const content="<article data-editorial-version=\"3\" class=\"sn-page\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">← Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine · Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/easy-inflatables/logo.webp\" alt=\"Easy Inflatables logo\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\"><h1>Easy Inflatables: dinghies and tenders for practical boating</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">Easy Inflatables sells Australian-designed Aerowave boats for tender duties, fishing and family outings. For owners of larger boats, a dinghy can be the equipment that gets used every day of a cruise, moving people and supplies between the vessel and shore.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/easy-inflatables/viper.webp\" alt=\"Aerowave Viper inflatable catamaran shown beside a tropical shoreline\" width=\"1200\" height=\"680\"><section><h2>Pick the small boat for its regular work</h2><p>Swift tenders, Viper and AeroCat catamarans and Sports Series monohulls provide different designs. Outboards and accessories are available alongside the hulls, allowing a buyer to consider the complete setup.</p><p>We like that the range covers more than one way to use an inflatable. A boat kept with a yacht and one carried to different launch places have different routines. Storage, carrying and typical loads help make the choice practical.</p></section><section><h2>Construction differences worth comparing</h2><p>Aerowave uses welded seams and pressure-relief valves. Viper and Sport models feature heavier VALMEX fabric for durability and abrasion resistance, while AeroCat uses lighter material to make carrying easier.</p><p>Those are identifiable benefits rather than vague descriptions of quality. We appreciate being able to connect the material choice to the use the boat will receive, especially when it will be lifted and handled regularly.</p></section><section><h2>Why we feature Easy Inflatables</h2><p>The range is designed on the NSW Central Coast and built offshore to the company&#x27;s specifications. The team includes commercial boating experience and focuses on useful small-boat applications.</p><p>We feature it because the tender has a direct job in making a cruising trip work. Owners who give careful attention to the main boat&#x27;s machinery can bring the same practical approach to choosing the smaller boat that carries the crew ashore.</p></section><div class=\"sn-contact\"><a href=\"https://easyinflatables.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Explore Aerowave boats ↗</a><a href=\"/supporters/\">More featured sponsors</a></div></div></article><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"Easy Inflatables: dinghies and tenders for practical boating\", \"description\": \"Explore Aerowave dinghies and yacht tenders from Easy Inflatables, with Australian design, welded seams and options for practical boating.\", \"image\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/images/supporters/easy-inflatables/viper.webp\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Marine Diesel Engine\"}, \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-05\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/supporters/easy-inflatables/\"}</script>";
